#nexus [SplitsTree6]

BEGIN SPLITSTREE6;
DIMENSIONS nDataNodes=10 nAlgorithms=6;
PROGRAM version='SplitsTree (version 1.0.0-SNAPSHOT) - License GPL v3';
WORKFLOW creationDate='1793974984427'; [Fri Nov 06 15:23:04 CET 2026]
END; [SPLITSTREE6]

[!Pararge aegeria rhabdovirus (PAegRV): the 131 sequences of Longdon et al. (2017), Proc. R. Soc. B 284:20162381, from the
authors' Figshare deposit DOI 10.6084/m9.figshare.3409420 (CC BY), collapsed to their 90 distinct haplotypes as File -> Open
Haplotype Data does (TYPEn names a haplotype shared by several sequences; the taxon info lists them), with the eight
sampling sites (six in Britain, Corsica, Sardinia) as traits with coordinates: see the trait pie charts and the world map.
RazorHaploNet with the Shave filter.]

[
Methods:
Analysis was performed using RazorNet (version dev)  (Huson and Bryant 2024 ; DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.).
The original input consisted of 90 taxa and 90 DNA sequences of length 1,281.
The Razor Haplo Net method was used (default options) so as to obtain 223 nodes and 322 edges.
The Shave Filter method was used (default options) so as to obtain 130 nodes and 138 edges.

References:
Huson and Bryant 2024: DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.
]

